# Code standards (mandatory)

- Prefer `const` constructors. Meaningful names. Small, focused classes.
- Performant: memory, rebuilds, high-frequency updates.
- Secure storage for sensitive data. Observable, debuggable code.
- Support iOS and Android (platform channels when needed).
- No hard-coded secrets, routes, colors, or text styles.
- No business logic in widgets. No API calls from UI or Blocs.
- No Flutter in Domain. No Riverpod as state. No god classes.
- No implementing from screenshots before Use Cases are approved.
- Prefer proven patterns over demos. Make reusable patterns explicit.
- Keep humans in the loop for regulated / money-moving decisions.
- Non-trivial or money-moving design: write a short design doc first. Say “I don’t know” or “I was wrong” and correct course.
